1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,290
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,290 --> 00:00:04,268
Your pipeline only helps
if it's kept up to date.

3
00:00:04,268 --> 00:00:09,069
In this lesson, you'll learn the everyday
moves: dragging deals, updating them,

4
00:00:09,069 --> 00:00:12,472
finding them quickly, and
changing lots of them at once.

5
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:16,314
Olivia has just replied
to our first message,

6
00:00:16,314 --> 00:00:18,900
so her deal is no longer a new enquiry.

7
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:22,414
Grab her card, and drag it
into the contacted column.

8
00:00:22,414 --> 00:00:25,995
The counts and totals at the
top update straight away.

9
00:00:26,846 --> 00:00:30,696
On a long board, or on your
phone, dragging can be fiddly.

10
00:00:30,696 --> 00:00:36,139
Instead, open the three dots menu on any
card, and choose the stage to move it to.

11
00:00:36,139 --> 00:00:38,529
Daniel's consultation is now booked.

12
00:00:39,379 --> 00:00:42,338
Ethan has accepted his
implant treatment plan.

13
00:00:42,338 --> 00:00:46,841
Click his card to open it, change
the status to won, and click update.

14
00:00:46,841 --> 00:00:50,057
Remember, it's the status
that your reports count.

15
00:00:50,907 --> 00:00:54,156
Noah has decided to stay
with his current dentist.

16
00:00:54,156 --> 00:00:58,185
Open his card, set the status
to lost, and pick a lost reason.

17
00:00:58,185 --> 00:00:59,550
Chose another clinic.

18
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:02,344
That reason will feed
your reporting later.

19
00:01:03,194 --> 00:01:05,810
To add a new deal, click Add opportunity.

20
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:07,278
Search for the contact.

21
00:01:07,278 --> 00:01:11,425
Jack Morris is back, and this time
he's interested in Invisalign.

22
00:01:11,425 --> 00:01:15,764
Finish the name, add the value, and
choose where the lead came from.

23
00:01:16,613 --> 00:01:20,300
Pipeline and stage are already
filled in, and the owner is you.

24
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:24,396
Click create, and the new deal appears
at the top of the first column.

25
00:01:25,248 --> 00:01:28,388
To find a deal fast,
type in the search box.

26
00:01:28,388 --> 00:01:31,029
Names, contacts and emails all match.

27
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:36,596
For more control, Advanced Filters narrows
the board by status, owner, source,

28
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:37,596
value or tags.

29
00:01:38,446 --> 00:01:42,546
I'll show just Sarah's deals, which
is great for a one-to-one with her.

30
00:01:42,546 --> 00:01:45,202
Apply, and the active
filter shows at the top.

31
00:01:45,202 --> 00:01:47,281
Click clear to see everything again.

32
00:01:48,131 --> 00:01:49,455
Prefer a spreadsheet?

33
00:01:49,455 --> 00:01:50,717
Switch to list view.

34
00:01:50,717 --> 00:01:55,321
You get every deal in one table, with
its stage, status, value and owner,

35
00:01:55,321 --> 00:01:56,961
and a total at the bottom.

36
00:01:56,961 --> 00:02:01,376
Click any row to open it, or use
Sort to put your biggest deals first.

37
00:02:02,227 --> 00:02:05,716
List view is also where you
change many deals at once.

38
00:02:05,716 --> 00:02:09,464
Tick the ones you want, and a
bar of bulk actions appears.

39
00:02:09,464 --> 00:02:14,116
James is off next week, so I'll
reassign two of his open deals to Priya.

40
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:19,248
You can also move stage, change
status, add a tag or delete in bulk.

41
00:02:19,248 --> 00:02:23,654
Every change is saved instantly, and
shows up on the contact's record,

42
00:02:23,654 --> 00:02:25,039
and on your dashboard.

43
00:02:25,039 --> 00:02:28,060
When you're done, switch
back to the board view.

44
00:02:28,911 --> 00:02:29,939
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:29,939 --> 00:02:34,112
Open the board first thing each
morning, and work from left to right.

46
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:36,591
Every card should have a clear next step.

47
00:02:36,591 --> 00:02:41,490
If a deal hasn't moved in two weeks, either
chase it today, or mark it abandoned,

48
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:43,183
so your numbers stay honest.

49
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:44,777
Nicely done!

50
00:02:44,777 --> 00:02:49,698
In the next lesson, we'll turn all this
activity into numbers: conversion rates,

51
00:02:49,698 --> 00:02:52,281
pipeline value, and where deals get stuck.

52
00:02:52,281 --> 00:02:53,142
See you there.
